<title>CHINA: Shanghai main air cargo route to China from Hong Kong.</title>
<headline>Shanghai main air cargo route to China from Hong Kong.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Eastern Airlines and Hong Kong's Dragon Airlines continued to dominate the route to Shanghai, the busiest air cargo route between Hong Kong and the rest of China during May, statistics published by the Civil Aviation Department show.</p>
<p>The carriers accounted for 2,175 tonnes of two way belly cargo during May.</p>
<p>Beijing was the next busiest destination for air cargo with 1,455 tonnes both inbound and outbound.</p>
